.TH HHC 1 "2026" "hhc" "H# compiler"
.SH NAME
hhc \- GCC-based compiler for the H# programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hhc
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR.h# ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hhc
is the GNU Compiler Collection driver for H#, the language of HackerOS.
It accepts the usual GCC driver options; H# source files use the
.I .h#
suffix.
.SH OPTIONS
Most GCC options work as documented in gcc(1), for example
.BR \-o ", " \-O2 ", " \-S ", " \-c ", " \-g ", " \-fsyntax\-only ", " \-x\ hsharp .
.TP
.B \-fhsharp\-dump\-ast
Print a short outline of the parsed program to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
hhc hello.h# \-o hello && ./hello
hhc \-O2 prog.h# \-o prog
hhc \-S prog.h#
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/hhc
Installation tree (compiler proper \fBhsharp1\fR, libgcc, start files).
.SH SEE ALSO
gcc(1), as(1), ld(1)
.br
https://github.com/HackerOS-Linux-System/hhc
